  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879712",
      "title": "Introducing Mutations - A Better Way of Changing Data",
      "lectureOrder": 216,
      "videoOrder": 189,
      "sourceHash": "8b1b9a66e1461b3d1e03080d19ce93ce3a34e482a63dcb6bd3c41b201f86497e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.32,
          "end": 4.21,
          "en": "Remember this slide?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.21,
          "end": 8.33,
          "en": "There I mentioned this predictable state management,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.33,
          "end": 12.14,
          "en": "this predictable flow, the clearly defined data flow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.14,
          "end": 16.22,
          "en": "which makes sure that we have to use a certain approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.22,
          "end": 17.64,
          "en": "of updating our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.64,
          "end": 19.36,
          "en": "and of getting our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.36,
          "end": 22.57,
          "en": "and this would be less error prone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.57,
          "end": 26.356,
          "en": "Well, actually, the way we're using Vuex at the moment works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.356,
          "end": 30.183,
          "en": "but it's not fully following the Vuex philosophy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.04,
          "end": 34,
          "en": "We're directly tapping into our store.state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "to change something from inside a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "and whilst this works technically here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 41.285,
          "en": "this is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.285,
          "end": 44.82,
          "en": "We can change the state from anywhere in the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.82,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "and it's up to us if we add one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 51.95,
          "en": "or if we set it equal to state.counter + 10",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.06,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "or we have a typo and accidentally type one twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 58.383,
          "en": "and hence add 11 every time we increment this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.3,
          "end": 61.72,
          "en": "So what I wanna say is that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.72,
          "end": 64.87,
          "en": "we still can introduce errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.87,
          "end": 66.32,
          "en": "because we're not having",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.32,
          "end": 69.16,
          "en": "a clearly defined state-changing mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.16,
          "end": 71.333,
          "en": "We can change the state from anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.47,
          "end": 75.72,
          "en": "That is why we should use Vuex a bit differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.72,
          "end": 78.83,
          "en": "We have this app-wide, central Data Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.83,
          "end": 80.36,
          "en": "this State Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.36,
          "end": 82.12,
          "en": "and we communicate with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.12,
          "end": 83.85300000000001,
          "en": "from inside our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.72,
          "end": 87.23,
          "en": "Now, I have a dashed arrow here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.23,
          "end": 90.13,
          "en": "because yes, we want to communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.13,
          "end": 91.81,
          "en": "but not directly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.81,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "What we're doing at the moment is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 98.663,
          "en": "Instead, Vuex has a built-in concept called mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 103.03,
          "en": "Mutations are clearly defined methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.03,
          "end": 106.38,
          "en": "which have the logic to update the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.38,
          "end": 108.44,
          "en": "And from inside our components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.44,
          "end": 112.03999999999999,
          "en": "we should, in the end, just trigger those mutations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.03999999999999,
          "end": 114.37299999999999,
          "en": "instead of directly manipulating the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.43,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "By triggering mutations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "all components that want to edit a state do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 122.66,
          "en": "in the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.66,
          "end": 125.523,
          "en": "And it's guaranteed that they do it in the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.49,
          "end": 128.35,
          "en": "And to give you an example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.35,
          "end": 131.243,
          "en": "I will actually add another component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.285,
          "end": 134.3,
          "en": "ChangeCounter.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.3,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "And this will be a very simple component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 137.84,
          "en": "which also just has a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.37,
          "end": 141.6,
          "en": "where I also say Add 1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 143.02,
          "en": "and where we're gonna click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.02,
          "end": 145.23,
          "en": "I want a trigger addOne.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.23,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "And then I have my script in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 149.61,
          "en": "And in there, my methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.61,
          "end": 153.12,
          "en": "where I have the addOne method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.12,
          "end": 156.35,
          "en": "And every component is able to use Vuex as you learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.35,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "So here I can access store.state.counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 160.623,
          "en": "and increment this by one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.06,
          "end": 165.287,
          "en": "Now, in App.vue, we can import ChangeCounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.279,
          "end": 169.779,
          "en": "and register it as a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.22,
          "end": 173.51,
          "en": "and use it in addition to the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.51,
          "end": 175.053,
          "en": "which we already have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.16,
          "end": 177.88,
          "en": "So I got two buttons now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.88,
          "end": 179.37,
          "en": "One here in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.37,
          "end": 180.923,
          "en": "and one in change-counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.95,
          "end": 184.94,
          "en": "Both should add one but here I'm adding 11",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.94,
          "end": 188.65,
          "en": "because I mistyped or I changed my logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.65,
          "end": 191.08,
          "en": "and forgot to rename the method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.08,
          "end": 192.62,
          "en": "and the text on the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.62,
          "end": 193.66,
          "en": "Whatever.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.66,
          "end": 195.46,
          "en": "But now we have two buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.46,
          "end": 198.88,
          "en": "One button adds 11 and one really adds one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.88,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, why am I doing this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.84,
          "en": "I want to show you that now we have different places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 203.84,
          "end": 206.21,
          "en": "in the app where we update our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 206.21,
          "end": 208.8,
          "en": "And even if we wouldn't have that stupid mistake",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 208.8,
          "end": 210.48,
          "en": "of having 11 here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 210.48,
          "end": 212.27,
          "en": "even if we would have one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 212.27,
          "end": 215.78,
          "en": "if we ever decide that we want to add two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 215.78,
          "end": 219.67000000000002,
          "en": "we have to change that in two components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 219.67000000000002,
          "end": 222.438,
          "en": "We have to go to two components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 222.438,
          "end": 225.06,
          "en": "and change our logic in two places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 226.09,
          "end": 227.56,
          "en": "and in bigger applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 227.56,
          "end": 229.4,
          "en": "we might have even more places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 229.4,
          "end": 232.03,
          "en": "where we need to change the logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 232.03,
          "end": 233.99,
          "en": "Now, that's a lot of code duplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 233.99,
          "end": 237.253,
          "en": "and that's exactly why we have this mutations concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 238.16,
          "end": 241.36,
          "en": "Back in main.js where we create our store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 241.36,
          "end": 243.36,
          "en": "we don't just have the state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 243.36,
          "end": 246.18,
          "en": "we also have mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 246.18,
          "end": 248.196,
          "en": "Mutations takes an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 248.196,
          "end": 252.01,
          "en": "and in this object, you can define methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 252.01,
          "end": 255.77,
          "en": "For example, I addOne method or increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 255.77,
          "end": 257.14300000000003,
          "en": "Whatever you wanna call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 258.06,
          "end": 260.92,
          "en": "And this method should contain the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 260.92,
          "end": 262.493,
          "en": "to change this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 263.55,
          "end": 266.61,
          "en": "Now, this method will automatically get the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 266.61,
          "end": 268.41,
          "en": "as a argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.41,
          "end": 270.72,
          "en": "This is guaranteed by Vuex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 270.72,
          "end": 272.49,
          "en": "Vuex will give us the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 272.49,
          "end": 274.34000000000003,
          "en": "whenever this method is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 274.34000000000003,
          "end": 276.98,
          "en": "and I will show you how to trigger such a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 276.98,
          "end": 277.823,
          "en": "in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 278.76,
          "end": 280.87,
          "en": "And since we get the current state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 280.87,
          "end": 283.32,
          "en": "the guaranteed latest state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 283.32,
          "end": 285.73,
          "en": "we can access state.counter in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 285.73,
          "end": 287.92,
          "en": "and increment this by one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 287.92,
          "end": 290.73,
          "en": "Also, of course, with this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 290.73,
          "end": 292.64,
          "en": "Or if we ever change our logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 292.64,
          "end": 294.023,
          "en": "we simply change it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 295.12,
          "end": 297.87,
          "en": "And now we want to trigger this mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 297.87,
          "end": 299.34000000000003,
          "en": "from all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 299.34000000000003,
          "end": 301.7,
          "en": "that should change our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 301.7,
          "end": 303.61,
          "en": "And of course, it should be needless to say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 303.61,
          "end": 305.77,
          "en": "that you can have multiple mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 305.77,
          "end": 308.853,
          "en": "You can have as many as you need for your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 309.8,
          "end": 311.17,
          "en": "So here I've got one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 311.17,
          "end": 314.25,
          "en": "and I wanna trigger it for the button in App.vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 314.25,
          "end": 316.67,
          "en": "and for the button in ChangeCounter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 316.67,
          "end": 319.98,
          "en": "Now, let's start with the button in ChangeCounter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 322.35,
          "en": "Here, to trigger a mutation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 322.35,
          "end": 325.02,
          "en": "we access this.$store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 325.02,
          "end": 328.61,
          "en": "but now there we've got a commit method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 328.61,
          "end": 329.95,
          "en": "It's a built-in method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 329.95,
          "end": 333.037,
          "en": "which Vuex gives you on its store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 333.037,
          "end": 336.137,
          "en": "And commit takes the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 336.137,
          "end": 338.83299999999997,
          "en": "of the mutation you want to perform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 340.28,
          "end": 342.73,
          "en": "In this case, that's increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 342.73,
          "end": 345.71,
          "en": "and the name should be provided as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 345.71,
          "end": 349.5,
          "en": "It's increment because I named my mutation increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 349.5,
          "end": 351.6,
          "en": "If you used a different name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 351.6,
          "end": 354.14300000000003,
          "en": "you also need to commit a different name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 355.27,
          "end": 359.49,
          "en": "But now we can commit this here in ChangeCounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 359.49,
          "end": 361.023,
          "en": "and also in App.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 362.25,
          "end": 364.26,
          "en": "And now we moved the logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 364.26,
          "end": 367.74,
          "en": "the concrete logic on how the state is updated out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 367.74,
          "end": 370.14,
          "en": "of the components into our store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
